 Open sessions are not held across view rendering (`spring.jpa.open-in-view` is disabled), so associations that a view needs are fetched eagerly at the mapping level.
 
+### View Templates
+
+Templates build links two ways. Expression preprocessing, written `__${...}__`, splices a value into the link expression before that expression is parsed. Link-expression parameters, written `@{/path(name=${value})}`, append the value as a URL-encoded query parameter.
+
+A request-derived value reaches a link only through link-expression parameters ([ADR](adr/2026-09-17-request-values-in-links-use-link-expression-parameters.md)). Preprocessing stays available for values the application itself computes, such as a page number.
+
+The paging links of the veterinarian directory carry the specialty filter under that rule `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+## Scale and Load
+
+Sizes and access patterns each path is designed against. A figure the project has not established is recorded as unrecorded and treated as bounded, and the simplest correct form is the design until an owner supplies the figure.
+
+| Path | Dominant operation | Realistic size | Access pattern | Form |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Veterinarian directory page, unfiltered | Paged read of every veterinarian | Seeded veterinarian and specialty counts are owned by `src/main/resources/db/{h2,mysql,postgres}/data.sql`; a clinic's real staff count is unrecorded, treated as bounded | Read-only, no write path in the application; results cached without eviction | Paged repository read at a fixed page size |
+| Veterinarian directory page, filtered by specialty | Paged read joined to the specialty a veterinarian holds | Bounded by the same staff count; each veterinarian holds few specialties | Read-only; caller supplies the filter text, so the key space is caller-controlled | Paged derived query, uncached ([ADR](adr/2026-09-17-filtered-vet-reads-bypass-the-vets-cache.md)) |
+| Machine-readable veterinarian list | Unpaged read of the whole collection, filtered or not | Same staff count; the whole collection is serialized in one response | Read-only; no paging on this form | Single repository read, serialized whole |
+| Owner search | Paged prefix read by last name | Unrecorded, treated as bounded | Read-only per search request | Paged derived query |
+
 ## Dependency Policy
 
 Minimize external dependencies. Every dependency is an attack surface and a maintenance burden.
